segments.source:
You probably learned in high school how to solve a system like
    <me>
      \syseq{
      x + 3y - z = 4;
      2x - y + 3z = 17;
      \. \+ y - 4z = -3\rlap.
      }
    </me>
    However, in real life one usually has to be more clever.

segments.translation:
아마 고등학교에서 <me>
      \syseq{
      x + 3y - z = 4;
      2x - y + 3z = 17;
      \. \+ y - 4z = -3\rlap.
      }
    </me>과 같은 연립방정식을 푸는 방법을 배웠을 것입니다. 그러나 실제 상황에서는 대개 더 영리하게 접근해야 합니다.

segments.source:
Sometimes the coefficients also contain parameters, like the <em>eigenvalue equation</em>
        <me>
        \syseq{
        (7-\lambda)x + y + 3z = 0 ;
        -3x + (2-\lambda)y - 3z = 0 ;
        -3x - 2y + (-1-\lambda)z = 0\rlap.
        }
        </me>

segments.translation:
때로는 계수에 매개변수가 포함되기도 하는데, <em>고윳값 방정식</em> <me>
        \syseq{
        (7-\lambda)x + y + 3z = 0 ;
        -3x + (2-\lambda)y - 3z = 0 ;
        -3x - 2y + (-1-\lambda)z = 0\rlap.
        }
        </me>이 그러한 예입니다.

segments.source:
Since the number of cars entering each intersection has to equal the number of cars leaving that intersection, we obtain a system of linear equations:
      <me>\syseq{
      w + 120 = x + 250;
      x + 120 = y + 70;
      y + 530 = z + 390;
      z + 115 = w + 175\rlap.
      }</me>

segments.translation:
각 교차로에 들어오는 자동차의 수는 그 교차로를 빠져나가는 자동차의 수와 같아야 하므로, 다음과 같은 연립일차방정식을 얻습니다. <me>\syseq{
      w + 120 = x + 250;
      x + 120 = y + 70;
      y + 530 = z + 390;
      z + 115 = w + 175\rlap.
      }</me>

segments.source:
The rules for reproduction lead to the following system of equations, where <m>x,y,z</m> represent the number of newborn, first-year, and second-year rabbits, respectively:
      <me>
\syseq{
    \. \+ 6y_{2016} + 8z_{2016} = x_{2017};
    \frac 12x_{2016} \+ \. \+ \. = y_{2017};
    \. \+ \frac 12y_{2016} \+ \. = z_{2017}\rlap.
  }
      </me>
      A common question is: what is the <em>asymptotic</em> behavior of this system?

segments.translation:
번식 규칙으로부터 다음과 같은 연립방정식을 얻으며, 여기서 <m>x,y,z</m>는 각각 갓 태어난 토끼, 한 살 토끼, 두 살 토끼의 수를 나타냅니다. <me>
\syseq{
    \. \+ 6y_{2016} + 8z_{2016} = x_{2017};
    \frac 12x_{2016} \+ \. \+ \. = y_{2017};
    \. \+ \frac 12y_{2016} \+ \. = z_{2017}\rlap.
  }
      </me> 흔히 묻는 질문은 이 시스템의 <em>점근적</em> 거동이 어떠한가 하는 것입니다.

segments.source:
Substituting the data points into the above equation yields the system
      <me>
\def\eqline#1#2{(#1)^2 + B(#2)^2 + C(#1)(#2) + D(#1) + E(#2) + F = 0}
\edef\eqs{\eqline02;
  \eqline21;
  \eqline1{-1};
  \eqline{-1}{-2};
  \eqline{-3}1;
  \eqline{-1}{-1}
}
\spalignsysdelims..
\expandafter\syseq\expandafter{\eqs\rlap.}
      </me>
      There is no actual solution to this system due to measurement error, but here is the best-fitting ellipse:
      <latex-code>
\begin{tikzpicture}[thin border nodes, whitebg nodes]
  \draw[grid lines] (-6,-4) grid (6,4);
  \draw[->] (-6,0) -- (6,0);
  \draw[->] (0,-4) -- (0,4);

  \point["{$(0,2)$}" above] at (0,2);
  \point["{$(2,1)$}" right] at (2,1);
  \point["{$(1,-1)$}" {right,yshift=-1mm}] at (1,-1);
  \point["{$(-1,-2)$}" {below,xshift=1.5mm}] at (-1,-2);
  \point["{$(-3,1)$}" {above,xshift=-1.5mm}] at (-3,1);
  \point["{$(-1,1)$}" below] at (-1,1);

  \draw[thick, seq-red] (-0.760768, -0.0153293)
      ellipse[x radius=2.61837, y radius=1.84472, rotate=26.0068];
  \node[text=seq-red, font=\normalsize] at (0, -3.3)
    {$266 x^2 + 405 y^2 - 178 xy + 402 x - 123 y - 1374 = 0$};
\end{tikzpicture}
      </latex-code>

segments.translation:
위 방정식에 데이터 점들을 대입하면 다음 연립방정식을 얻습니다. <me>
\def\eqline#1#2{(#1)^2 + B(#2)^2 + C(#1)(#2) + D(#1) + E(#2) + F = 0}
\edef\eqs{\eqline02;
  \eqline21;
  \eqline1{-1};
  \eqline{-1}{-2};
  \eqline{-3}1;
  \eqline{-1}{-1}
}
\spalignsysdelims..
\expandafter\syseq\expandafter{\eqs\rlap.}
      </me> 측정 오차 때문에 이 연립방정식에는 실제 해가 존재하지 않지만, 가장 잘 들어맞는 타원은 다음과 같습니다: <latex-code>
\begin{tikzpicture}[thin border nodes, whitebg nodes]
  \draw[grid lines] (-6,-4) grid (6,4);
  \draw[->] (-6,0) -- (6,0);
  \draw[->] (0,-4) -- (0,4);

  \point["{$(0,2)$}" above] at (0,2);
  \point["{$(2,1)$}" right] at (2,1);
  \point["{$(1,-1)$}" {right,yshift=-1mm}] at (1,-1);
  \point["{$(-1,-2)$}" {below,xshift=1.5mm}] at (-1,-2);
  \point["{$(-3,1)$}" {above,xshift=-1.5mm}] at (-3,1);
  \point["{$(-1,1)$}" below] at (-1,1);

  \draw[thick, seq-red] (-0.760768, -0.0153293)
      ellipse[x radius=2.61837, y radius=1.84472, rotate=26.0068];
  \node[text=seq-red, font=\normalsize] at (0, -3.3)
    {$266 x^2 + 405 y^2 - 178 xy + 402 x - 123 y - 1374 = 0$};
\end{tikzpicture}
      </latex-code>
